 "path": "memory/arc-grid-divider-copy.md",
 "content": "# ARC pattern: divider-framed pattern repetition\n\nEvidence from solved task-f36417f3 (2026-09-29): A grid used a background color with a full-height vertical divider at column 9, another at column 19, and full-width horizontal divider at row 6. The colored marker pattern in the top-right 6x9 cell region (rows 0-5, cols 20-28) was the source. The output copied that pattern into all other 9x6 regions of the 3-column by 2-row layout, keeping divider lines intact. In the demonstration (9x17), divider col 8 and row 4; source pattern was top-right 4x8 region, copied into top-left and repeated into both lower regions. Background and divider colors vary between instances. Procedure: identify full row/column separators; take non-separator cell as source; extract the populated tile bounded by dividers; repeat source tile into the other tile positions, maintaining the separator color and background. Verified output was accepted correct.\n"
